{"gap_id": "GAP-025", "category": "RP", "priority": "P1", "status": "OPEN", "description": "BATCH 17 MINING ASSIGNMENT — owner instruction 2026-09-18, answering GAP-022: \"then assign the mining for the next batch\". THE MECHANISM FOR \"runs eventually\" IS ASSIGNMENT, NOT AN AGEING METRIC. GAP-022 named the missing half of the 2026-09-18 ruling (deferred is okay so long as it runs eventually) and proposed building an age or backlog measure. The owner answered by assigning the work instead, which is the cheaper and more honest instrument: a deferral runs because a batch is told to run it, not because a counter goes red. DERIVE THE BACKLOG, NEVER QUOTE IT -- select slug, global_ref_id, deferred_reason from citation_mining where deferred_reason is not null; measured 2026-09-18 at ten rows, all on accessible-circulation-geometry. BATCH 17 TAKES THESE, IN THIS ORDER, AND THE ORDER IS REASONED. (1) REF-01002 backward -- the highest-value target on the slug by its own framing, a 2009 study saying design recommendations for either the running slope or the cross slope requirements are based on limited empirical research, so it cites whatever empirical work existed. BLOCKED BEHIND GAP-016: no DOI, therefore no Crossref deposit, so its reference list can only come from the article, which GAP-016 must obtain anyway to settle C10. Reading it discharges both. (2) REF-00979 backward -- ranks second on the GAP-018 predictor (a paper cites the literature of its own independent variable; Chow et al. measure propulsion across a slope series), and mining it is therefore also a PROSPECTIVE TEST of that predictor, with the prediction already recorded in its deferral note before the pass. (3) REF-00980 backward -- a 1997 paper cites pre-1997 work, and the pre-1997 ramp-slope literature is exactly what REF-01002 abstract calls limited; expected yield modest, stated in advance. (4) REF-00983 and REF-00986 backward -- batch 08 deferrals, the oldest in the register, and REF-00986 own extraction is graded absent so its references are unlikely to be gradient-bearing; both cheap. (5) REF-00999, REF-01000, REF-01001 backward -- T3, so R2 depth-2-3 obligation over CONFIRMED T1-T2 anchors reaches them only secondarily; take them only if capacity remains. (6) REF-00989 and REF-00993 FORWARD -- both Japanese-language, no DOI, absent from every citation index, so the forward graph does not reach them. THESE TWO ARE NOT A MINING PASS AND MUST NOT BE DRESSED AS ONE: the tractable equivalent is a Japanese-language site search for organisations quoting the same framing, which is a SEARCH and is recorded as owed. WHAT DISCHARGE REQUIRES: a pass that runs clears its deferral only with --discharge-deferral, which asserts the standing deferral belongs to the direction just run; without it the deferral stands and log-mining prints deferral_still_standing. Batch 17 closes this gap by emptying the backlog or by re-deferring with fresh reasons -- never by silence.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:04", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-16-backward-mining-t2-anchors", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 21:04", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-16-backward-mining-t2-anchors"}
