{"gap_id": "GAP-026", "category": "RP", "priority": "P1", "status": "OPEN", "description": "GAP-016 IS NOT CLOSED: REF-01002 FULL TEXT IS UNOBTAINABLE BY EVERY ROUTE AVAILABLE TO THIS ENVIRONMENT, MEASURED ACROSS SEVEN. Batch 17 was convened to read it and could not. Routes, all persisted as artefacts: academia.edu 403 on two different copies, researchgate 403, JSTOR 200 whose body is a bot interstitial, SafetyLit 503 then empty, OpenAlex 429 with the environment budget exhausted. THE INFORMATIVE ONE IS CROSSREF: a bibliographic title search returns five neighbouring papers and not this one, which VERIFIES rather than assumes the no-DOI fact the whole problem rests on -- Journal of Architectural and Planning Research never deposited it. Consensus returned the record and the same abstract, corroborating existence at index level, not full text. WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE DETERMINATION, UNCHANGED AND SAID AGAIN BECAUSE IT IS THE POINT: extraction 45 stays skim/preliminary, REF-01002 stays UNVERIFIED, gate 1 stays open, C10 keeps refusing the re-determination, parameter 3 x MOB stays undetermined. WHAT WOULD ACTUALLY WORK, and none of it is a search: a library or document-delivery route (JSTOR institutional access, ILL, or a request to the corresponding author, whose consultancy publishes its papers). THAT IS A DIFFERENT KIND OF WORK FROM A RETRIEVAL LADDER and the next batch should plan it as such rather than re-running the same seven routes and recording a second null. AN OPEN METADATA QUESTION RIDES ALONG: TRID prints the fourth author Weiner, Jerome M; a search summary rendered it Welner, J. M. Neither is a retrieved authoritative index. The stored author row says Weiner and is UNCONFIRMED -- settle it with the same retrieval that settles the rest.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:21", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 21:21", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17