{"gap_id": "GAP-027", "category": "RP", "priority": "P2", "status": "CLOSED-DECIDED", "description": "GAP-018 PREDICTOR PASSED ITS FIRST PROSPECTIVE TEST, 19 AGAINST A PREDICTED FLOOR OF 8 -- AND ONE PASS IS NOT A RESULT. The predictor: a paper cites the literature of its OWN INDEPENDENT VARIABLE, so what an anchor MEASURES predicts its backward yield better than what it is ABOUT. Batch 17 pre-registered a falsifiable floor for REF-00979 (Chow et al., propulsion across a slope series) in two places committed before the pass -- the batch-16 deferral note and this batch priors file -- stating that fewer than 5 matches would WEAKEN the predictor. Measured: 19 of 30. REF-00980 (Sanford 1997) returned 5 of 25 against a prior of 0-2, low on count and exactly right on character. RUNNING TALLY, derive it rather than trusting this line: REF-00985 slope-series biomechanics 23/46, REF-00979 slope-series biomechanics 19/30, REF-00977 effects review 6/117, REF-00980 threshold test 5/25, REF-00984 instrument review 0/38. WHAT IS STILL OWED BEFORE THIS BECOMES DOCTRINE: GAP-018 asked for three or four prospective passes and this is ONE. The two remaining assigned deferrals that can test it are REF-00983 and REF-00986, both slope-adjacent biomechanics, so the predictor says both should yield -- record a floor for each BEFORE the pass. A WEAK INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION arrived unasked: REF-00979 and REF-00985 reference sets OVERLAP on the 1989 portable-ramp paper (10.3109/03790798909166390), which is what the predictor implies two same-variable anchors should do. Weak because two papers in one small literature will overlap anyway; recorded so it is not later mistaken for a second test.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:21", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 22:09", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining"}
