{"gap_id": "GAP-028", "category": "EG", "priority": "P1", "status": "OPEN", "description": "THE PRE-1990 RAMP-GRADIENT LITERATURE HAS NO DOIs, AND IT IS WHERE THE 1:12 THRESHOLD PROBABLY COMES FROM. REF-00980 backward pass returned five relevant references, every one pre-1997 and NOT ONE carrying a DOI: a 1957 study to determine the specifications of wheelchair ramps; a 1971 architectural movement study whose Part 3 is titled Ramp gradients; a 1979 accessible-buildings study; a 1981 Dutch paper on accessibility by means of ramps; a 1993 review of technical requirements for ramps written as an RFP attachment. THIS IS A SYSTEMATIC PROPERTY, NOT BAD LUCK, and it now has three independent demonstrations in this corpus: REF-01002 (2009, no DOI, invisible to six batches of DOI-keyed searching), candidates 102 and 103 from batch 16 (no DOI in their deposits), and this entire pre-1990 layer. EVERY SEARCH METHOD THIS PROJECT USES IS DOI-KEYED OR INDEX-KEYED, so the foundation layer of its central parameter is structurally out of reach. WHY IT MATTERS RATHER THAN BEING AN INTERESTING FACT: REF-01002 abstract asserts that design recommendations for running slope and cross slope REST ON LIMITED EMPIRICAL RESEARCH. That is a checkable claim about a NAMED set, and this batch has now named it. If the 1971 Ramp gradients study is the measurement behind 1:12, the codes are anchored; if it is not, they may never have been, and a finding that a code is insufficient is first-class evidence under the 2026-09-13 ruling. EITHER ANSWER IS A RESULT. Closing this needs a library or archive route, the same non-search work GAP-016 now needs, and the two should be planned together.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:21", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 21:21", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining"}
