{"gap_id": "GAP-029", "category": "RP", "priority": "P1", "status": "OPEN", "description": "THE GAP-018 PREDICTOR IS FALSIFIED, AND THE RESULT REPORTED AS ITS FIRST SUCCESS WAS A SCREEN ARTEFACT. THIS RETRACTS A CLAIM MADE EARLIER IN THIS SAME BATCH. The predictor: a paper cites the literature of its OWN INDEPENDENT VARIABLE, so what an anchor MEASURES predicts backward yield better than what it is ABOUT. TWO PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTIONS, BOTH FAILED, IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS. REF-00983, whose independent variable IS ramp slope, predicted >= 8 and returned 2 of 23 -- its references are the TRANSIT-VEHICLE and ADA-guidelines literature, because a reference list follows the papers FIELD and problem framing, not its independent variable. REF-00986, whose independent variable is activity type, predicted <= 4 and returned 9 of 45. Both failing in opposite directions on one test is the hypothesis being wrong, not noise. THEN THE SCREEN WAS TESTED AND IT IS CONFOUNDED, which is worse. The screen regex carries propuls and accessib, so ANY wheelchair-propulsion paper matches regardless of slope content. Under a STRICT slope-only screen (ramp|slope|incline|gradient|grade|cross-slope): REF-00986 falls 9 to 0 of 45; REF-00979 falls 19 TO 2 OF 30. REF-00979 IS THE 19-OF-30 THIS BATCH REPORTED AS THE PREDICTORS FIRST PASSED PROSPECTIVE TEST, in a commit message, a session record and a PR body. It was counting cites wheelchair-propulsion papers, which is trivially true of a wheelchair-propulsion paper. NOTE WHICH ANCHOR SURVIVES THE STRICT SCREEN BEST: REF-00980, 4 of 25, the one I predicted LOW -- its hits are genuinely ramp-titled. So the strict screen inverts the original ranking as well. WHAT IS NOW OWED: (1) GAP-018 and GAP-027 are superseded by this row; do not cite either as support. (2) Every yield figure this project has recorded for a mining pass used the loose screen and is an OVERCOUNT of slope relevance -- re-derive with the strict screen before quoting any of them. (3) If a predictor is wanted at all, the candidate the data now suggests is FIELD AND PROBLEM FRAMING rather than independent variable, and it must be pre-registered and tested the same way rather than adopted because it fits five retrospective points.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:37", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 21:37", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining"}
