{"gap_id": "GAP-030", "category": "SW", "priority": "P1", "status": "OPEN", "description": "GAP-008 HAS NOW BLOCKED THE SAME ADMISSION TWICE, AND THIS BATCH HAS THE CONCRETE PROOF OF THE CORRUPTION RATHER THAN THE PATTERN. Rouvier et al. 2022 (10.1371/journal.pone.0269657, PLOS ONE, open access, 76 references deposited) was retrieved and verified through Crossref this batch and COULD NOT BE ADMITTED. add-source refuses under R9 because the DOI is filed in source_locators as REF-00037 and R9 says cross-file rather than duplicate. REF-00037 IS CORRUPT IN A WAY THAT MAKES THAT INSTRUCTION DESTRUCTIVE: its doi column holds the PLOS ONE identifier while its title column reads Inclusive Housing Design Guide. RIBA/Habinteg/CAE. DOI:10.4324/9781003564164, authors Runnalls and Walker, year 2024 -- a different work, with a different DOI sitting inside the title text. REF-VERIFIED-003 holds the same DOI with title, authors and year all NULL. So R9, applied to a corrupt stash, directs an admission onto a mismatched identifier and would carry the corruption into evidence_sources. THIS IS THE SAME SHAPE THE 2026-09-16 RETIRE-IN-PLACE RULING RECORDS from batch 08, one row-state along: there, thirteen RETIRED tombstones were read as live DOI claims and the only remedy offered was to cross-file a retired identifier; it was fixed by exempting RETIRED rows. REFERENCE-ONLY rows whose DOI does not match their own title are the unfixed member of that class. WHAT IS MISSING AND WHY NOTHING WAS FORCED: update-locator writes status only; the vocabulary is REFERENCE-ONLY, PROMOTED, SCREENED-OUT, RETIRED, and none of them honestly states this row DOI does not belong to its title -- SCREENED-OUT asserts a lead was worked and judged unacceptable, which is false here, and would also bury a housing-guide lead whose own title and authors look sound. Hand SQL was not used (CLAUDE.md section 4). PROPOSED, NOT BUILT: a correct-locator that reads doi and title from a persisted retrieval payload and takes no value flag, the way correct-source does -- which is what source_locators_integrity has been asking for at advisory level while this defect blocks admissions at blocking level.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 21:38", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 21:38", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining"}
