{"gap_id": "GAP-032", "category": "SW", "priority": "P3", "status": "OPEN", "description": "B06 KEEPS A CURATED gaps.status LIST THAT IS NARROWER THAN THE COLUMN OWN CHECK, AND I TRIPPED IT. The column CHECK permits anything LIKE OPEN% OR LIKE CLOSED%; test_db_integrity B06 enumerates a fixed tuple. Closing GAP-018 and GAP-027 as CLOSED-SUPERSEDED -- accurate, and accepted by the writer and the column -- turned a BLOCKING check red at 73/74. Resolved by using CLOSED-DECIDED, a ratified value that fits (both were closed by the decision recorded in GAP-029), rather than by widening B06, because adding a value to a check to accommodate a value I had just invented is the shape of disabling a test to get green. WHAT IS ACTUALLY OWED: B06 is a curated vocabulary sitting beside a column that declares its own, which is CLAUDE.md rule 8 (never curate a fact the machine can compute) in a test file. Either B06 derives from the column CHECK, or the column CHECK is tightened to the enumerated set and B06 reads it -- the present arrangement means a writer and a blocking check disagree about the vocabulary, and the disagreement is only discoverable by tripping it. Note CLOSED-SUPERSEDED is the semantically right value for a superseded gap and the project has no way to express it.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 22:09", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 22:09", "updated_by_session": "session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining"}
